Barack Obama wins Nobel Peace Prize as the Fourth U.S. president
U.S. President Barack Obama flocks to Oslo, Norway, at 26 a.m. in order to accept the Nobel Peace Prize as the fourth U.S. president in history.
Among other things, it will receive a miplom, a medal and a $1.4-mortgage for exceptional efforts to boost world diplomacy and cooperation between nations.
The head of the White House will come to the Norwegian metropolis in the morning with his wife Michelle and he will be busy.
At first, he goes to a Nobel institute, where for the for the first time he will meet five members of the committee, which in October he was selected from 172 people and 33 organizations.
The presidential couple is then scheduled to meet King Haraldo V of Norway and Queen Sonja.
Afternoon, a visit culminates in a ceremonial ceremony, at which Obama will receive a prestigious award.
It will be won by the Fourth U.S. president, but only the third to receive the award directly in office.
The White House has already announced that Obama will speak of an Afghan war while accepting the award.
The president does not want to espouse this issue because he realizes that he receives the prize as a president who is currently fighting in two countries.
A few days a few days a few days ago, he increased his efforts by sending additional troops to Afghanistan, not forgetting to highlight any of his critics.
During the ceremony, Obama will also receive a gold medal, a diploma and a cheque for ten million Swedish kroner (approximately $24 million).
He intends to put them for charitable purposes, but he hasn't already made a specific charity.
The contracted program will then be introduced by the president with his wife to the banquet, where, in addition to the Norwegian king and the queen, there will be a ministerial presiding chairman and 250 other invited guests.
From the outspoken price, Obama has restrained.
He stated, for example, that he feels that he did not fully deduce it.
He also repudiated several times that it is not only the price for him, but for all those who strive for the same values as him.
Immediately after announcing, he said he was a "calibration for action."
