U.S: Repetition Is the Mother of Wisdom
It is almost comical, with what school-spirituation Barack Obama, the president with the reputation of the smartiest, repeats in the Afghan question the strategy of his predecessor, whom he himself regarded as the dumbest.
When he finally shoved his long-awaited Afghan Doctrine, it emerged that he copied it through a copier from the Bush Iraqi Scream three years ago.
Not only does he use the phrase “just like in Iraq” several times in the text itself, but he did not hesitate to even use the name of Bush’s January 2007 statement as the name of his own declaration: “A new way forward”.
Three years arguing three years ago, he criticized Bush's idea of sending fresh military reinforcements to Iraq plagued by civil war as "an irresponsible and in its aftermath of catastrophic decisions."
In subsequent months, however, have shown that the Bush strategy based on the recommendations of field commanders was the only possible and very successful thing so that there is no talk about Iraq at all today.
It didn't improve Bush's repudiation, but he objectively left his successor with a much more grateful starting situation than could be expected.
In Afghanistan, Barack Obama hopes to reciprocate the miracle.
He was reapplied by field commander-in-culpture commander-in-chievement of the Afghan operation General Stanley McCistal, who, despite subordination habits, harshly criticized the hesitant shooters in the White House, have asked him to increase the military contingent.
He demanded 40 thousand men to be able to break the situation for the better.
The president was hesitant for three months, but he didn't fall for anything better, so at least he cheated the general by 10 thousand soldiers.
From Europe he was able to squirm the promise of another 5,000, even though he himself originally counted on at least 10.
The most questionable thing about Obama's entire strategy appears to be his inquistion to start withdrawing troops out of Afghanistan in as early as 18 months and end this process within three years. The entire Obama doctrine raises more questions than it provides answers.
Many have in doubt that a halved increase will give the same fruit as advancement in Iraq.
Despite fratricidal wars in recent years, Iraqi society is relatively well-arranged, its leaders honor the agreements.
The Afghan Situation is characterized by the opposite symptom - no one can be relied on and no agreements are respected.
Under these conditions, the Afghan security forces accustomed to regenerating the master every day according to how it suits them.
Political institutions, even if formally established, will remain only a potemkin village under which patriarchal tribal relations will continue to flourish.
Balancing the interests of various ethnic groups is extraordinarily complex due to the confluence of circumstances that complicate Pakistani and Iranian influences even further.
Even building an "accomplable state", which is a minimalist goal of the entire operation, doesn't seem very realistic.
The time horizon of Obama's strategy is striking by its voluntarism.
In the last eight years, the situation in Afghanistan only deteriorates and is now on the verge of an explosion.
Believing in the fact that soldiers sent into the turmoil for the purpose of "an early return home" will cause a miracle made here, only a truly romantic soul, untouched by reality.
From the political point of view, the determination of the date of the withdrawal of troops is pure irresponsibility, because the Taliban will perceive this as an indirect admission of American defeat.
NATO's latest summit has shown that the willingness of Europeans to participate in combat operations in Afghanistan is laundering.
European politicians can’t and don’t even want to explain to their constituents how the security of Germany or Italy is related to the Hindu shut-to-foot war.
Another illustrative being able to radically intervene in the situation is the development of events around Iran.
“While the situation continues to deteriorate and intensified sanctuaries doesn’t impermeate Iranians, there will be a hard question in front of the United States whether to try to solve the problem by military force.
It will be responsorored at a time when, according to Obama, America will proceed to the victorious withdrawal from Afghanistan.
However, each such solution will also mean a dramatic turnaround in an Afghan situation.
The only patch for Barack Obama is the fact that there are three years left until the presidential election, so there is still plenty of time left for him to come up with another strategy, as long as this turns out to be a total flop.
Goldman Sachs bank executives won't get cash rewards
The senior executives of Goldman Sachs won't receive cash rewards this year.
This was announced by the company, which thus responds to sharp criticism of its wage practices.
