Israeli Ada Jonath was awarded the chemia prize, along with the Americans Venkatraman Ramakrishnan and Thomas Steitz for clarifying the structure and function of the ribosomes.
The last laureate had the Nobel Prize in Economics, which was won by American Elinor Ostrom and her compatriot Oliver Williamson for his analysis of economic governance.
The only professional category that took place without a holder this year was physics.
This award was awarded today by Charles Kao scientists for optical fiber research and George Smith with Willard Boyle for the insuing CCD chip, the basis of all digital cameras, faxes or astronomical telescopes.
Each honoree received a diploma, a Nobel Medal and a certificate of profit of a financial reward.
