According to the new ČD order, there will be fewer trains for almost the same fare
As of December 13, Czech Railways will cancel or limit some less used express trains and locals, while others will strengthen the connections.
From the date of validity of the new timetable, the overall scope of transport will be reduced by two per cent compared to today.
Most fares, including basic and customer fares, do not change.
For example, the inhabitants of the Ostraava region will get more possibilities of connection to the capital city, the railways on this track will add to one pendolino set.
On the contrary, the fast train stops coming to Bratislava.
Fewer fast trains will also ride on the line Praha - Písek - České Budějovice, fundamentally limited direct connections Prague - Letohrad.
Of the regions, the railways plan the largest reduction of traffic in the Hradec Králové region, by a total of eight per cent, on the contrary, Prague and its surroundings can look forward to an increase.
There are also two night trains on the route Prague - Tábor - Ceske Budejovice and the operation of a few express trains on the line Prague - Písek - České Budějovice is limited only to some days of the week.
One of the biggest changes is the introduction of a new direct line from Milovice to Prague, today Milovické must transfer in Lysá nad Labem.
It is the 15th line of suburban Esko, its opening is possible thanks to the completion of electrification of the line from Lysá nad Labem to Milovice.
Long-distance connections to the capital city will end at the destination station Prague Main Railway Station.
ČD introduces more SC Pendolino connections between Prague and Ostrava and trains to Šumperk/Jeseník will run at two-hour intervals.
As of December 13, passengers will no longer take a ride through Pendoline in Bratislava.
