This year, regional trains are 200 million more expensive.
For locals and express trains, the tracks have a newly concluded ten-Year-year contract, so far the contract has always been for one year.
The railways commute the system, which is why they apparently did not reach an increase in the prices of the vast majority of tickets.
There will only be any changes for one-daiday ČD Net network tickets and inexpensite eLiška online tickets.
For passengers without a customer card, the price of ČD Net will increase from 450 crowns to 600 crowns.
The price of eLiška will newly depend on the distance traveled, hitherto been unsolute for the journey between arbitrary regional towns and amounted to 160 crowns.
