A transformer for tens of millions of kroners is on fire in Louny
The fire engulfed a transformer of Čeps in the morning in a subsidy near Výškov in the Louny region.
Lukáš Marvan, a spokeswoman for regional fire brigadiers at the blaze, intervening six units, according to Lukáš Marvan.
Originally, the firefighters wanted to let the transformer burn out, but later they reconsidered the opinion and the fire extinguishes with a mixture of water, foam and special extinguishing agents.
The cause was a technical glimpse, an internal short-circuit of the transformer.
No one was injured, according to company spokeswoman Pavla Mandátová, the accident does not jeopardize the safe operation of the transmission system.
Damage is estimated at several tens of millions of crowns, accurately quantifying it can be quadrupled after the end of the fire.
Destroyed transformer, according to Mandátová, will need to be replaced with a new one.
In the ten-year operation of Čeps, nothing similar has happened, glitches of this type are unique, she supplemented.
According to a spokeswoman for CEZ for Northern Bohemia Soni Holingerová Hendrychová, the supply of electric currents has not been interrupted, the functioning of households, authorities or companies did not affect the fire of the transformer station.
A.s. Čeps acts on the territory of the Czech Republic as an exclusive operator of the transmission system, power lines 400 kV and 220 kV.
It maintains, renews and develops 39 substations with 67 transformers converting electrical energy from the transmission system to the distribution system and the power lines with a length of 4339 kilometers.
