UDF raises the tone and urges the Nouveau Centre party to no longer enjoy their abbreviation.
UDF-controlled by MoDemFrançoise Bayrou on Friday responsored an attempt by Nouveau Centre's president, Hervé Morin to appropriate the abbreviations of Giscard's former party, not using the abbreviation abbreviation in any medium under the threat of criminal charges.
Hervé Morin has publicly announced his intent to appropriate an abbreviation UDF, stating that François Bayrou didn't devour her inheritance after he handed over to the left.
The defense minister, whose party is a UMP partner, planned to certify this strategy on Saturday before the Nouveau Centre (NC).
His move received support from MP Hervé de Charetto (former za-UMP now for NC), who attributes the ownership of the UDF brand, because he was the first to register it in 2004 at the National Institute of Industrial Property (l'Institut national de la propriété industrielle).
But on Friday evening, the UDF-based committee of friends of François Bayrou who does not intend to expropriate himself, resigned from his silence and filed a formal request to the minister and deputies to stop using an abbreviation abbreviation and return the ownership of the trade mark, under the threat of criminal prosecution.
In recent days, you've increased the troubling statements about proposing to your political movement + re-acquire the UDF abbreviation UDF, the association writes in a letter signed by 19 of the 24 members of the committee, such as François Bayrou and Marielle de Sarnez by MoDem or senator Jean Arthuis of Alliance centriste.
At the same time, you considered it advisable to place on your promotional materials and on the welcoming website of your movement the name +Nouveau center+, with the slogan +UDF of today +UDF +UDF today+, the signatories of the letter will also state.
As you are aware, you do not have the right to use this abbreviation, the UDF committee, which asks the NC"immediate to remove all references of the UDF name from all promotional materials, including (of its) websites.
At the same time, he asks Hervý de Charette " to hand over the ownership of a trade mark to legitimate owners".
If you do not do so, we will go to the courts in order to respect the law and the legitimate rights of UDF members, the signatories point out.
In their letter, they state that UDF "is a full-bodied political movement since 1978 "and recall that Mr. Morin and his friends "choose "left in 2007 , "to create a non-competition movement, just like others in 2002, to establish an UMP.
The Nouveau centre movement therefore does not have, according to them, any right to use the abbreviation UDF (Union pour la démocratie française).
At the same time, they commemorately observe that the last UDF Congress voted in 2007 to join MoDem for three years and for the creation of a committee authorized to defend "moral and material interests" association established by Valéry Giscard d'Estaing.
Regarding Hervé de Charette, the committee continues, "when he registered a trade mark", he wasn't "for three years a UDF member," but UMP.
In a scalable and scuggabling manner, he took advantage of non-existent acronym registration to do so at his own expense.
This tactlessness begins to be transformed into a criminal offense, deceivered, and then with irony they comment on the NC strategy: "They seem to us that, both in politics and in everyday life, it is more matterable to create a name for yourself than to withdraw from an anonymity by deceiving a name to which we have no right".
Liliane Bettencourt: François-Marie Banier will be tried for abusing a state of weakness.
The court in Nanterre on Friday ruled that François-Marie Banier gave rise to whether he took advantage of the ten-year-old billion-year-old weakness to deprive her of a portion of her fortune acquiring her daughter Liliane Bettencourt, of which he is accused by her daughter Liliane Bettencourt.
