Because they're graduates of colleges for engineers, they have a mechanical interpretation of psychology.
Due to thought-compactness, they acquire an old behaviorist theory, currently reinvigorated by "neurosciences" from the U.S and widely disseminated without greater knowledge by scientific institutions and the media.
With the fact that it is possible to be able to move the "leaves" (sic) the involvement of managers was demonstrated by a recent Ipsos poll on Figaro.fr, which only reaffirms executives in their position of mechanical management, unsuitable for today's world.
Identify and measure factors of mobilization.
Concurrence, the managerial revolution necessary for the proper functioning of modern enterprises presupposes the acceptance of the final vision of human behavior.
It consists in incorporating basic insights into all the intentions and practices of management : Commitments to an undertaking will only be possible for employees if they appear as a clear means of attaining their dreams, ambitations and projects.
At present, this concept of employee motivation is dealt with only studies of Motivationally functional analysis.
These studies have shown that they evaluate their businesses on the basis of predetermination of a predetermination basis that will enable them, through an image that testifies about the enterprise, to evaluate what it offers them to realize their life goals.
Thanks to the identification and measurement of these Mobilization factors, managers can control, anticipate, and anticipate on "social performances" and put their human resources management "on the right path".
This creates a breeding ground for the development of solid and effective economic intelligentsia.
Speaking from Oslo: "fair war" Obama earned praise from the right.
The U.S. right welcomed a speech by Barack Obama on Friday the day before in Oslo, satisfied that the 2009 Nobel Peace Prize winner defended the concept of an "just war" against the enemies of the United States.
Conservatives, who initially mocked the Obama Award on October 9 applauded a presidential speech, including Sarah Palin, a former 2008 vice-presidential nominee in the 2008.
I liked what he had said, Palinová, the muse of the right-of-wing Republican Wing, told USA Today, adding that she herself "sometimes the necessary" war commented on this topic in her memoirs, which are just coming out.
