Speech from Oslo should serve as a guide to international decisions in resolvability of conflicts, combating poverty and oppression," the California daily inflamed.
Obama "he gave a speech as it took," the New York Times said, calling the speech "simple and innocuous."
Road hauliers: three marathons to an agreement that will save the supply of supplies for Christmas.
After three negotiating marathonuments, the unions of road hauliers and TLF ran out, the only Employ Employer's organization that remained until the end, on Friday evening for an agreement that ended the call for the strike and the threat that hung over the supply of supplies for Christmas.
Treasury Secretary-Stutic Dominique Bussereau expressed "joyness" at Friday's signing of the deal after several negotiations that began on Wednesday morning.
After the second night of discussions, the negotiators dispersued early in the morning with the hope that the wording of the agreement would be signed as quickly as possible at the end of the morning.
That’s despite the fact that the three employers (FNTR, Unogra, OTRE) withdrew from the negotiations.
But there was a need for another more than six hours of the meeting, which began at 11 a.m. in order for everyone to make an adequake and signed an agreement at 6 p.m.
This conflict "would hurt businesses very much" and "thousone would be in danger of disrupting the holiday at the end of the year," Bussereau said.
The text contains an increase in wages of 4% for the lowest salaries (in local and regional road transport) and 2.9% for the highest salaries (international transport).
An hourly wage for the lowest salaries increases from €8.72 to €9.06.
It's not a lot, but there is a lot of effort behind it, Patrice Clos (FO explained).
Tonight, we're going to instruct our members to avoid blockades, there's no resuppliing detention centres.
But there may still be a few opponents who are unsatisfied "he added.
Philippe Grillot, the president of the TLF, welcomed the "right deal," although it was hard to admit an increase in high salaries due to an international competition."
According to him, there will be an increase of 170 euros per month for the lowest wages and by 100 to 120 euros for the highest.
It is an agreement of common sensuousness and respect for employees, CMaxime Dumont (CFDT) said, while Thierry Douine (CFTC) welcomed a "historical deal."
Richard Jaubert (CGT), it is an "acceptable compromise."
The agreement also enviscases revaluing travel expenses of 3% and a report on the situation of road transport in the first half of 2010, which will also allow a focus on the issue of the 13th salary and the modernisation of a collective agreement.
Bussereau recalled "reducing €100 million in corporate salaries" that was the subject of the government's amendment to the 2009 bill on the budget for 2009, which the National Assembly voted on last night from Thursday to Friday.
The government will ask the senate "congruous" vote.
The signature allows this agreement to apply first to enterprises that are members of this organization, later to the entire field, in the event of an extension by the Ministry of Labour.
It will take place "in the shortest possible time", Bussereau assured.
The whole process can be hindered only by the disagreement of employers' organizations.
FNTR talks about "bad trade" because 100 million euros "has already been offered to the sector as part-of-compensation of part of the carbon tax".
The Secretary of State for Transport Forced us to act not as a result as a result of mutual analysis, but in order not to annoy thrift eaters of turquits at the time of the upcoming Christmas holidays, Unostr complained.
For Otre, there is a risk that an agreement will "burbury a large number of small and medium-size enterprises in the field" in the next 12 months.
