75% of working mothers have maternity-related work problems.
Discrimination in employment has increased in recent years, especially for women of younger vintage who are going to get a child.
This is the result of the study 'Ferciseness and the working career of Spanish women', which was carried out by CSIC in cooperation with the Women's Institute.
9,737 women between the ages of 15 and 75 took part in the study and the results are unequivation: 75% of working mothers have limited opportunities in the labour market due to maternity.
The study emphasizes that at the beginning of cohabitation there are many differences in opinions on the number of children depending on whether or not they work, as well as according to the type of employment.
Women who don't work away from home, work part-time or don't have a stable job, start living with a partner earlier, previously give birth to their first child, and generally have multiple children.
On the other hand, women with a stable job, especially in the public sector, postpone cohabitation and maternity, and have fewer offspring.
"Women from 35 to 49 years of age with a stable job have an average of 3.7 years since cohabitation with a partner. This figure amounts to 4.1 in the case of women who have devoted a greater part of their lives to achieving their stable job and therefore had to decomminting their cohabitation and the arrival of children.
The type of profession also has a strong effect on maternity, albeit a minor influence on the start of cohabitation with a partner", explains Margarita Delgado, which is engaged in research at CSIC.
Another factor influencing the age of women at the time of the marriage of an arrogance of the offspring is the level of education.
The research shows that the higher the level of education, the higher the age when women get married and have their first child.
Distingunciations are also between women of the same generation.
For example, in an age-accurrant group of 35-49 years of age, women gave birth to their maternity child at the age of 25.1 or 32.1.
"There is another difference between women depending on their level of education.
Women with basic education get married and give birth to the first child before they find a stable job, while women with secondary or high-education advancing in the opposite preference for obtaining a stable job, before marrying and the birth of the first child," Delgado said.
