Cowardly Aggression
Last week my 70-year-old-year-old mother went through our neighborhood, Fuenlabrada, and a group of young people between the ages of 15 and 18 went for a walk and our dog, a junction rescued from a shelter weighing no more than six kilos, without a sing-spoke, kicking it twice and severely injured.
Our indignation is all the greater because we don't see anything fun in such an affliction towards a small and defenseless animal, which, moreover, was on a leash.
On top of that, an old mistress's shock after this incident, when she clashed with these individuals on a walk, she began to worry about her own safety, because such a devil-obsessed person who attacks an animal is able to do the same to a woman, a child, an old man or anyone who is weaker than himself.
It happened at five o'clock in the afternoon, Tuesday, in a usually quiet neighborhood.
The dog we cried all day.
Of course, we have filed a complaint against the nearest commemorative commemorations, but we doubt that it was useless and in order not to provoke delicate questions, we note that these cowardly murderers were of Spanish nationality.
Indecency has prompted us to announce this fact.
We do not understand what is going on with today's youth when they are amused by bothering a defense-free animal, which gives us love, society and friendship.
We don’t understand where the proper upbringing, respect for animals and humans has gone.
Michelin and Fesvial together for using helmets
Tire maker Michelin, in cooperation with the Spanish Transport Safety Foundation (Fesvial), has launched a campaign to promote the use of helmets, mainly among younger motorists, as both subjects reported today.
The purpose of this initiative is to emphasise the importance of the use of the helmet, since it is the only means to prevent head injuries or deaths in the event of an accident while riding a motorcycle.
Michelin submits that this campaign forms part of their obligations relating to traffic safety, which "means more than to design and produce even safer products", and has confirmed that it seeks to fulfil this purpose otherwise, i.e. in the form of an instructional and information campaign.
This new campaign to promote the use of a helmet when riding a motorcycle, under the motto 'To be or not to be', is the first stage when up to more than 500 motorcycle-refurbishments will be deployed signboards in order to come to the attention of the general public.
Finally, Michelin pointed out that traffic safety "is a constant problem" of this company, which is a manufacturer of tires for two-wheeled vehicles and whose main objective is to continuously increase product safety.
Increasing sales of light commercial vehicles
After almost two years, the market of light commercial vehicles is beginning to recover.
All 9.4,425 vehicles registered in Spain meant an increase of 12.6% compared to 2008 and what's more, it is the first increase after 22 months of sustained bankruptcy, according to the figures of the patronage organization of Anfac manufacturers and sellers Ganvam.
Favorable, however, it is better to quarantine, because November 2008 is a very bad period for comparison and meant a 60% reduction compared to the previous year.
Responsibility for this, despite the rise in the last month, the total number of registered vehicles in the last 11 months accounts for 40% less than in the previous financial year.
Since January, 95.853 vehicles have been sold, which includes all possible vehicles belonging to the category of light commercial vehicles: passenger car derivatives, pickups, vans, smaller trucks and light trucks/chairs.
And the gloom has not disappeared, which is most damaging to demand, even if they were bought by private individuals, most purchases were carried out by small and medium-sized firms, and in 100% of cases it is financing through third parties.
Other factors, such as cessation of an activity or a continuation of a bad economic situation, must also be added to the restrictions resulting from the closure of the source of bank loans.
In this situation, as opposed to passenger cars, support for the purchase of 2000E did not help very much.
In Addition to private individuals, it is necessary to mention io-business-business-making companies, which intend to purchase a light commercial vehicle of up to 3.5 tons with a CO2 emission level not exceeding 160 grams per kilometer, but the number of operations has been confirmed.
It was yesterday from Ganvam that it is necessary to pay special attention to the management of these vehicles, as well as industrial vehicles (cars and buses).
An association of sellers assumes that in 2010 the development will be similar as last year and, according to calculations, sales for passenger cars and 4x4 will fall by 19%.
An auxiliary system for handbrake is already mandatory equipment.
As in the case of an anti-blocking ABS system, it will also deal with ESP stability controls, all this will become the mandatory equipment of European cars.
In fact, it already forms part of the mandatory equipment of all newly registered passenger cars and light-duty commercial vehicles, while for the others there is a deadline to eliminate the shortage, which is February 2011.
Measures introduced in the EU aim to increase the protection of pacifiers, functioning in such a way that it can help to avoid much rainfall.
Auxiliary hand-brake system increases pressure on the brakes in an emergency case, which the system detects when the driver presses.
But it doesn’t always maintain that pressure until the end.
According to a study carried out by car parts maker Bosch, one-thousuous of drivers who have an injury didn't stop the brake from the collision, and half of them didn't take full advantage of the brake's strength.
Up to 1,100 Accidents
On the contrary, this assistance requires the maximum from the braking system, shortens the braking distance of the vehicle.
According to a study carried out in the EU alone, if all the vehicles were equipped with this type of equipment, up to 1 100 fatal accidents a year-on-affiliated could be avoided.
Resuing this number will be even more pronounced according to co-quots would be avoided by one of the four accidents with an impact on the person-after the introduction of so-called intelligent hand-brake systems.
In this case, the vehicles will be equipped with a system that (using a radar or camaraderie) will catch obstacles and report them to the driver, in addition to light braking.
If the driver responssibly responds, it will help him increase the pressure on the pedal if it is needed.
