New tools for valuing cars
During these days they are storming and accidents are profiting not only by car repair shops.
Every day thousands of cars that suffered an insured event are towed to the service, where an expert must estimate the damages and the cost of the repair.
No insured event is the same, and the calculation of the cost of the parts and the time of the workforce can be a long and complex work.
Calculate manually the cost of repair from 20,000 to 30,000 euros, including parts and workforce, can take two or three hours.
However, with the support of new computer tools it would be a matter of minutes
That's why almost 100% experts use this kind of system.
Service providers and solutions for estimating claims and maintenance are dedicated to the collection of information provided by the manufacturers to then develop and to offer their customers a useful tool.
In Spain Audatex, from the U.S. Soera group is a leading company; 80% evaluation is carried out with its products.
GtMotive and Eurotax are other companies that compete in the fields of valuation and elaboration of sector information.
Working with data provided by manufacturers is not easy at all.
According to Eduard Velázquez, Sales Director of Audatex, in Spain they work with 63 manufacturers and importers, each of which provides them with information in a different format.
In addition, the amount of processing data continues to grow, as in the last five years there have been more versions, variants and motor solutions than in the previous fifteen years.
As soon as the new vehicle enters the market, these businesses will start to work.
It is a very feverish work, because it is necessary to catalogue each of the thousands of parts of the vehicle and determine its price.
In addition to each model, "intelligent" graphics are carried out, where it is possible to "puncture" individual parts of tourist cars.
When it comes to the model with a massive sale, the work can be done in a week if the process is very fast.
When it comes to a millennium car, it can take three or four months. At present, Audatex has at his disposal complete information about 99.2% of cars sold in Spain.
The most excclusive models they have information about are Porsches, for example, not Ferrari or Lamborghini.
Regarding the mobile park in circulation exceeds 99%.
In order to carry out the work of documenting and elaboration of databases, Audatex has eight center-divided in the world (Spanish, France, Germany, USA, Brazil, Mexico, China and Japan) and each of them specializes in specific brands.
The national seat is in Alcobendas (Madrid).
There more than a hundred technicians (numally experts in mechanics) work at the same time with three computer screens.
Audatex invests €90 million per a year in the elaboration of these databases.
Each month 2.5 million data is included and customers receive updates every two days.
The processing of this immense stream of information allows companies to make different uses and the provision of different products.
The most frequent use is focused on repairs and maintenance, but according to individual countries, there are also tools to control spare parts or to calculate the selling or residual value of a car.
The only undertaking at its disposal to have a guide that informs about the value of used vehicles in Spain is Eurotax.
Audatex doesn't offer them in our country, but they don't in the United States.
Taking Into account the Audatex products, it's easy to get support that professionals in the sector can take advantage.
This company offers ten different tools, the stellar product being AudaPlus, a standard invening valuation solution for connoisseurs.
Include automobiles, motorcycles and light and heavy-duty industrial vehicles.
In Addition to the cost of the parts, it also includes the time for repairs estimated by the manufacturer or varnish.
This tool shall be applied according to the application for each evaluation.
The highest price is €5.75 for customers who use it little, no more than ten times a month.
Thereafter, each insurance company carrying out thousands of estimates will negotiate its price with Audatex.
Other products such as AudaVIN make it possible to fully Identify the vehicle and the equipment with which it came out of the assembly line only on the basis of the first undercarriage number.
AudaGlass concentrates on vehicle glasses and AudaSubastas is an open service to the professional sector on the Internet, which makes it possible to disable vehicles with an overall insured event.
Its statistical service is very useful for determining the tendency, performing geodemographic analyses, or detecting deviations according to brands or models.
For example, it is possible to study how many models of a particular brand have been serviced due to an accident or how many serious inefficiencies suffered over a certain period.
Gt Motive is the only Spanish company dedicated to the development of this type of tools.
Among other things, it sells Gt Estimate, which is also intended for connoisseurs and also provides digital images, access to parts or prices and official times of the manufacturer.
Gt Motive is an Einsa group company founded in 1971 as a supplier of services and solutions for the assessment of damages, accidents or car maintenance
Gt Guía Valuation is its reference historical product on the market.
They work with 24,000 users in services, 3,100 experts and 53 insurers.
The turnover volume increased by 20% a year over the past three years, accounting €10.8 million in 2008.
At the beginning of the last year began the process of internationalizing the installation of an office in Paris.
Audatex originated in Germany in 1966 and established itself in Spain in 1979.
According to the company's sources, 62% of its brother is created in Europe and 38% in North and South America. She works with 900 insurance companies and 33,000 of them services, of which 3,000 in Spain.
Solera (Audatex (Audatex, Sidexa, Informex ABZ, Hollander and IMS) will reach $557 million, 3.3% more than in 2008.
In our country, the company earns 19.1 million euros, which is 7.2% more than last year.
In 2005, Solera Group cost $1,000 million on the stock exchange, and its shares are now estimated at an all-period of $2,4,900 million.
It has been quoted on the New York Stock Exchange since 2007 and is included in the Standard & Poor's reference index.
Internet Audaction of Crashed Vehicles
Last October, Solera Groups bought Autoonline, an internet base for the sale of cars and motorcycles or special vehicles after an insursing event.
The operation anticipated the signing €59.5 million from 85% of the company's 85% capital, which could expand by the remaining 15% next year.
The aim of the purchase was to provide value-added services to customers with the possibility of accessing a huge international market.
This Valuation and Purchasing/SALES service is guaranteed exclusively to professionals in the sector, such as insurance companies, connoisseurs, borrowers, spare parts sales and professional resellers who have to register prior to the commencement of operations.
Established in 1996 in Germany and manages more than 650,000 surgeries across Europe, of which 500,000 in Germany.
Among the main markets, Spain, Greece, Poland and Turkey stand out.
The website currently has more than 1,500 registered sellers and 4,000 connoisseurs.
It manages 3,000 daily adverts, and about 100 new adverts every day are added on the Spanish market.
According to the Spanish law, the car whose chassis number has been decommissioned cannot go into service, but it can be used as a source of spare parts that have not been damaged.
Cars with a historical value may be authorised, although they have been disqualified, after preliminary proceedings.
Debaversation budget in four steps
With Auda-Taller, Audatex guarantees that the user receives a budget only in four steps: identification of the vehicle, finding a spare part, creating a budget and generating a budget.
Ease of application is an essential condition for these systems, especially for the beliefs of professionals at an older age who, to a greater or lesser extent, restrain when using new management techniques.
The database contains 1,014 vehicles, including 666 hiking, 109 off-road, 137 motorcycles, 78 vans and 44 trucks.
Naturally you need a computer with an internet connection.
After Identification of the model to be repaired using the chassis number, a real graphical view of the model will appear, and then the necessary spare part will be selected.
The user can include the variables as the price of the workforce, surcharges or discounts, and then print and hand it over to the customer.
AudaTaller isn't an appreciation tool like AudaPlus, it's a reference catalog.
The main difference between the two systems is that service-driven and doesn't include workforce estimation.
The cost of using this workshop tool is €350 per annum, which can be financed by the customer.
Audatex is currently working to ensure that these impressions are three-dimensional.
This is an innovation that mechanics welcome, because it will allow you, for example, to choose a door and rotate them in order to display the inner side.
